--
--   Description
-- 
-- This tests ensures that the GEM deals with collisions properly in 
-- both normal gigabit mode and burst gigabit mode.
-- 
-- Functional coverage
-- -------------------
-- � Ensures that early collisions are detected in both normal gigabit 
--     mode and burst gigabit mode.  
--     i.e. Tests for collisions during preamble and SFD in normal 
--           gigabit mode.
--          Tests for collisions during preamble and SFD within a burst 
--           of frames in burst gigabit mode.
--          Tests for collisions during crc in both normal gigabit 
--           mode and burst gigabit mode
-- � Tests for collisions during carrier extension in normal gigabit mode.
-- � Tests for collisions during inter-packet gap (IPG) within a burst.
-- � Tests for late collisions during carrier extension in burst gigabit mode.
-- � Tests for collisions during padding in both normal gigabit mode and 
--     burst gigabit mode.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 
-- In Normal Gigabit Mode:
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for gigabit operation.
-- 2. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision at 
--     the beginning of preamble (2nd byte).
-- 3. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     towards the end of preamble (6th byte).
-- 4. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     in the  (8th byte) start of frame delimiter (SFD). 
-- 5. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     at the start of the carrier extension (64th byte).
-- 6. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     at the start of the carrier extension (65th byte).
-- 7. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     towards the end of the carrier extension (512th byte).
-- 8. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     in the beginning of the data portion of the frame (24th byte).
-- 9. Transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--     towards the end of the data portion of the frame (58th byte).
-- 10. Transmit a minimum sized frame with padding plus extension with 
--      a collision at the start of the padding (36th byte).
-- 11. Transmit a minimum sized frame with padding plus extension with 
--      a collision towards the end of the padding (50th byte).
-- 12. Transmit a minimum sized frame with extension with a collision at 
--      the start of crc (61st byte).
-- 13. Transmit a minimum sized frame with extension with a collision 
--      towards the end the crc (63rd byte).
--      
-- In Burst Gigabit Mode:
-- 14. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension.  
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision at the 
--      beginning of preamble (2nd byte).
-- 15. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision towards 
--      the end of preamble (6th byte).
-- 16. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision in the  
--      (8th byte) start of frame delimiter (SFD).
-- 17  In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension.
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with a collision 
--      just before the start of the interframe gap (64th byte)
-- 18. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension 
--      with a collision at the start of the interframe gap (65th byte).
-- 19. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension with 
--      a collision towards the end of the frame extension (512th byte).
-- 20. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision in the 
--      beginning of the data portion of the frame (24th byte).
-- 21. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision towards 
--      the end of the data portion of the frame (58th byte).
-- 22. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame plus extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with padding with a collision 
--      at the start of the padding (36th byte).
-- 23. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with padding with a collision 
--      towards the end of the padding (50th byte).
-- 24. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame with extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision at the start 
--      of crc (61st byte).
-- 25. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame with extension. 
--      Then, transmit a minimum sized frame with a collision towards the 
--      end the crc (63rd byte).
-- 26. In burst mode, transmit a minimum sized frame with extension. 
--      Then, transmit a collision between the first frame and second 
--      frame (IFG). Finally, Transmit a minimum sized frame.
-- 27. Check statistics
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

